.  IP \(bu 2.3
.\}
all selected Notes in applied order
.br
The list of \*(Aqenabled Notes\*(Aq includes all Notes from \*(Aqadditional
enabled Notes\*(Aq and additional all the Notes related to the \*(Aqenabled
Solution\*(Aq too. The list shows the order in which these Notes were
applied and will be re\-applied after a system reboot, if the
\fBsaptune.service\fP is enabled.
.RE
.sp
.RS 4
.ie n \{\
\h'-04'\(bu\h'+03'\c
.\}
.el \{\
.  sp -1
.  IP \(bu 2.3
.\}
all currently applied Notes in applied order
.br
The list of \*(Aqapplied Notes\*(Aq includes the \fBmanually\fP applied Notes.
Additional it includes all the Notes related to the \*(Aqconfigured
Solution\*(Aq too. These Notes get applied when using \*(Aq\fIsaptune solution
apply\fP\*(Aq. The solutions and their related notes can be listed by
\*(Aq\fIsaptune solution list\fP\*(Aq.
+
And additional \*(Aqapplied Notes\*(Aq shows if the system is \*(Aq\fBactively\fP\*(Aq
tuned at the moment. If the list is empty, the system is \fBnot\fP tuned.
If the list is \fBnot\fP empty, the system \fBis\fP tuned.
